  "Id": 1334,
  "Title": "English for Work course",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "A big congratulations to the first group of participants who successfully completed the English for Work course!",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The main aim of the English for Work course is to provide participants with a language-rich environment in order to develop their skills in English for work-related situations. It was delivered via face-to-face classroom teaching and an integrated online component. \n   "
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "\n      The class was divided into two groups, in order to provide more individualized attention and to cater better for each participant's level of English development. The participants were confident and very eager to learn and improve their English. They attended the face-to-face classes with great zeal and wanted to practise their English at every opportunity."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "\n      This course is offered twice a year and has limited seats available. One of the main features of this course is the British Council, LearnEnglish Select online learning component. These materials are specifically designed to develop English language skills for work purposes."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "\n      "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Here is some feedback from two of the course participants:",
